# The server's texts (MD_ in SRVSCR.C, the status screen, and in SRVRUN.C,
# the failures said on standard error once this file is loaded).
# Format: "nnn NAME text", the source format (see SRC/CLIENT/MSG.H); ^1
# and ^2 take arguments.
# The title and the uptime share the top row.
# W=55 title, with a name of NB_NAMELEN - 1: VID_COLS - SS_UPW - 1
1070 MD_TITLE RETROINV server ^1
# W=24 uptime, with ^1 at most "49710d 23:59:59": SS_UPW
1071 MD_UPTIME Up ^1
# W=21 MD_UPTIME's ^1: SS_UPW - 3
1072 MD_DAYS ^1d ^2
# W=19 labels of the settings rows: SS_VAL - 2
1073 MD_DATA Data directory
1074 MD_RO Read-only stations

# W=59 a settings value: VID_COLS - SS_VAL
1075 MD_NONE none
# W=19 labels of the settings rows: SS_VAL - 2
1076 MD_OPEN Sessions open
1077 MD_LISTEN Waiting for calls

# W=79 VID_COLS - 1
1078 MD_NOSESS No session is open.
# Column headings, each at most as wide as its column.
# W=4 SS_SLOTW
1079 MD_COLSLOT Slot
# W=4 PROTO_KINDLEN
1080 MD_COLTYPE Type
# W=16 ENG_STALEN
1081 MD_COLSTA Station
# W=8 ENG_USERLEN
1082 MD_COLUSER User
# W=5 SS_LVLW
1083 MD_COLLVL Level
# W=18 SS_STATEW
1084 MD_COLSTATE State
# W=13 SS_IDLEW
1085 MD_COLIDLE Idle
# Session states (PROTO_S_NEW .. PROTO_S_CLOSED).
# W=18 SS_STATEW
1086 MD_STNEW connected
1087 MD_STHELLO logging in
1088 MD_STMUSTCHG changing password
1089 MD_STREADY ready
1090 MD_STCLOSED closing
# The trace row: MD_TROFF or MD_TRON, then the trace events
# (CONN_EV_OPEN .. CONN_EV_CLOSE), ^1 the slot.
# W=79 the trace row: VID_COLS - 1; MD_EVOPEN..MD_EVREQ's ^2 (a station, a user, a request line) is cut at the row
1091 MD_TROFF Trace off
1092 MD_TRON Trace on
1093 MD_EVOPEN Slot ^1 opened from ^2
1094 MD_EVLOGIN Slot ^1 logged in as ^2
1095 MD_EVREQ Slot ^1: ^2
1096 MD_EVCLOSE Slot ^1 closed
# The bottom row; MD_YESNO holds the capital letters that answer MD_ASK,
# yes then no.
# W=79 VID_COLS - 1
1097 MD_HINT F2=Trace  F3=Shut down  F5=Refresh
1098 MD_ASK Sessions open: ^1.  Shut the server down?  Y=Yes N=No
1099 MD_YESNO YN
1100 MD_STOPPING Shutting down: waiting for the sessions to end
# SRVRUN.C: failures on standard error, after "INVSERV: ".  They are
# lines of the console, not drawn in a slot of fixed width: no W=.
1101 MD_NODATA cannot open the data directory: ^1 (error ^2)
1102 MD_NOLOG cannot open the event log ^1 (error ^2)
1103 MD_NOMEM not enough memory for the sessions
1104 MD_NAMEUSE the name ^1 is in use
1105 MD_NONAME cannot add the name ^1 (NetBIOS error ^2)
1106 MD_NOSCREEN cannot set up the screen
1107 MD_NOCLOSE cannot close the data files (error ^1)
1108 MD_NOLOGW cannot write the event log ^1 (error ^2)
1109 MD_STUCK ^1 NetBIOS commands pending; waiting (any key ends the wait)
1110 MD_NOPORT there is no serial port COM^1
1111 MD_PORTUSE the serial port COM^1 is in use
1112 MD_NOMBOX cannot find the mailbox ^1 or its REQUEST and RESPONSE directories
# The serial ports' rows and the mailbox's row, below the sessions.
# W=19 labels of the settings rows: SS_VAL - 2
1120 MD_SERIAL Serial ports
1121 MD_MAILBOX Mailbox
1122 MD_PORT COM^1
# The ports' column headings, each at most as wide as its column.
# W=5 SS_BAUDW
1123 MD_COLBAUD Baud
# W=6 SS_CHIPW
1124 MD_COLCHIP Chip
# W=7 SS_ERRW
1125 MD_COLOVER Overrun
1126 MD_COLFRAME Framing
1127 MD_COLPAR Parity
1128 MD_COLLOST Lost
# Chips (UART_T_8250 .. UART_T_16550A).
# W=6 SS_CHIPW
1129 MD_C8250 8250
1130 MD_C16450 16450
1131 MD_C16550 16550
1132 MD_C16550A 16550A
